{
  "$comment": "REMOTES (#EXP-1613; src/remote.ts, ecode-core remote.rs). `parse`: `https://host[:port]/a/b[.git]` → {scheme, host (lowercased), path (no `.git`, no trailing slash)}; `exp://<team>/<repo>` → eCode's own (exactly one path segment); anything else is null: http, ssh, scp-style, credentials or a query in the URL, `.`/`..` segments. `helperKey` = the git config key that scopes the device's credential helper to EXACTLY that https remote (`credential.https://host/path.git.helper`), so a token never reaches another host; exp remotes authenticate inside `git-remote-exp` and get none. `refresh`: a token is refreshed when it expires within contract remote.refreshMarginMs (null = never expires). `redact`: every non-empty secret, longest first, becomes contract remote.redaction in any text a runner or git call logs.",
